Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:02:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 703/703] SableOS: single-key mute, speaker and dialpad on the in-call
 screen

For phones with a hardware keyboard (Q25): during a call that is
active, on hold or dialling out, with the dialpad hidden, M toggles
mute, S toggles the speaker and D opens the dialpad.

* Never while a call is ringing, so no key answers or rejects.
* With the dialpad open letters stay DTMF digits (W E R = 1 2 3 on a
  phone-pad keyboard), unchanged.
* Held keys and keys with Shift, Alt, Sym, Ctrl, Meta or Fn keep the
  upstream meaning.
* S does nothing when Bluetooth is a route: the on-screen picker
  chooses between three routes.

The decision is the pure SableInCallKeys class; host tests live in the
SableOS Q25 repository under tests/framework/packages/apps/Dialer.
